{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.zeta4_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.zeta4_sq","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L215-L222","doc":"Derived (proved, conditional on the class): each composite's assembled\nfibre object satisfies `ζ₄² = −1` — the two-rotation negation, obtained\nfrom the conjectural faithfulness field alone (via\n`IsZeta4Faithful.zeta4_sq`). Confirms the class asserts genuine content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L213-L213","doc":"the open physical content: each composite's assembly is ζ₄-faithful. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly.mk","kind":"ctor","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L211-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.SingleFrakVAssembly","kind":"class","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L199-L213","doc":"**Single-`𝔙` assembly conjecture (§3b `Prop`-class; conjecture — no\ninstance is provided).** The OPEN piece of the `𝔙` fibre-descent (the 5nx8\ngap map's OPEN item): that the actual binding + `Q_β` observables of a\ncomposite `K` assemble into a *single* complex fibre object\n`frakV : K → ℂ → ℂ`, and that this physical assembly is **ζ₄-faithful**\n(supported on the two faithful `±i` characters — the falsifiable\nconstraint). Following the repo §3b convention (`ComplexVolumeFibre` in\n`ComplexVolumeFibreDescent.lean`), the assembly is a **parameter** and the\nclass is `Prop`-valued (a pure logical assumption, no computational\ncontent / multiple-instance ambiguity); its single field is the open\nphysical hypothesis. No instance is given (the physical match is open).\nNon-degenerate: the structural consequence `ζ₄² = −1` is derived below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.IsZeta4Faithful.zeta4_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.IsZeta4Faithful.zeta4_sq","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L188-L197","doc":"**Derived (sorry-free): ζ₄-faithfulness forces `ζ₄² = −1`.** Adding the\norbit-sum and sign-isotype vanishing gives `A z + A(z + 2·iπ/2) = 0`, i.e.\ntwo ζ₄ rotations negate the assembly — recovering `vModel_zeta4_sq` from\nfaithfulness *alone*, for any faithful `A`. This is the class's genuine\nprovable content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_isZeta4Faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_isZeta4Faithful","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L182-L186","doc":"**Non-vacuity: the `cosh + i·sinh` model is ζ₄-faithful.** Direct from the\nproved orbit/sign-isotype vanishing lemmas — the constraint is realisable,\nso the conjecture below asks for something possible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.IsZeta4Faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.IsZeta4Faithful","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L171-L180","doc":"**ζ₄-faithfulness predicate.** A candidate assembly `A : ℂ → ℂ` is\nζ₄-faithful iff both non-faithful `ℤ₄` isotypes vanish: the full ζ₄-orbit\nsum (trivial isotype) and the alternating orbit sum (sign isotype) are `0`,\nso `A` is supported on the two faithful `±i` characters. The falsifiable\nconstraint on the open single-`𝔙` assembly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.zeta4Rot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.zeta4Rot","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L166-L169","doc":"The `ζ₄ = i` rotation of the fibre argument, `z ↦ z + iπ/2` (reducible, so\nit is definitionally the inline form used by the proved orbit/sign lemmas\nabove). Names the term the ζ₄-faithfulness constraints iterate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_eq_faithful_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_eq_faithful_sum","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L135-L142","doc":"**Faithful decomposition.** The model is exactly the sum of its two faithful\nζ₄-eigencomponents: `V₀(z) = (1+i)/2·e^z + (1−i)/2·e^{−z}` (eigenvalues `+i` / `−i` by\n`exp_zeta4_eigen` / `exp_neg_zeta4_eigen`). The binding and Q_β channels are the\nsymmetric/antisymmetric recombinations of this faithful pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.exp_neg_zeta4_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.exp_neg_zeta4_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L126-L133","doc":"`exp(−z)` is the `−i`-eigenvector: `exp(−(z + iπ/2)) = −i·exp(−z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.exp_zeta4_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.exp_zeta4_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L116-L124","doc":"`exp` is the `+i`-eigenvector of the ζ₄ rotation: `exp(z + iπ/2) = i·exp z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_sign_isotype_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_sign_isotype_zero","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**Sign isotype vanishes**: the alternating orbit sum is zero — the model has no component in\nthe sign character of `ℤ₄` either. Together with `vModel_orbit_sum_zero`, the model is supported\nentirely on the two FAITHFUL characters `±i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_orbit_sum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_orbit_sum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L95-L103","doc":"**Trivial isotype vanishes**: the full ζ₄-orbit of the model sums to zero — the assembly\ncarries NO ζ₄-invariant component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_cube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_cube","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**ζ₄³ = channel conjugation**: three rotations send `V₀` to `cosh − i·sinh` (Q_β channel\nnegated, binding channel kept — the partner relation's mirror). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_sq","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**ζ₄² = −1 on the model**: two rotations negate `V₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_partner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel_zeta4_partner","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L55-L65","doc":"**ζ₄-partner relation.** The `ζ₄ = i` rotation `z ↦ z + iπ/2` sends the complex-volume model to\n`V₀(z + iπ/2) = −cosh z + i·sinh z` — it **negates the bar-even (binding / Re) channel** and keeps\nthe bar-odd (Q_β / Im) channel. This is the fibre-level signature of how `ζ₄` couples the two\nchannels of `𝔙 = Vol + i·CS`. (For real `η` the RHS is `−conj V₀(η)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.vModel","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ComplexVolumeZeta4Partner.lean#L30-L31","doc":"The complex-volume fibre model on a complex argument: `V₀(z) = cosh z + i·sinh z`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}